Z||000021||Ken Wittlief||06-15-2001||04:08 PM||||This is easy:<P> they want someone who will ask THEM what they want<P>  and will LISTEN to THEM<P>    and who will then give them what THEY want, not what you THINK they want.<P> the hardest part is sometimes they dont think you will give them what they want, or they dont think you have it within you to give them what they want, so instead of telling you what they WANT, they tell you what they think they have to settle for.<P>  here is a personal example. When I got married I had just gotten out of the Coast Guard (4 years), was planning on going to college, my father had recently died, and I was pretty much broke, had no job, no money, and nobody to go to for help.<P>  When my wife and I discussed our wedding plans we decided to have a small wedding and take a simple honeymoon, not very far from home.<P>  It wasnt till years and years later that my wife told me she really wanted a big formal wedding, and she really wanted to go to Hawaii for our honeymoon, but since she knew I had no money or job at the time, and I was going to college soon, it wasnt possible.<P>   thing is, if I had known that at the time, if had known this was something she really wanted, I would have found a way. We could of put the wedding and college off for half a year, I could of gotten a temporary job or two, even if it was something difficult or something I hated, you can put up with just about anything for a few months, I could of pulled it off, the whole nine yards.<P>  and if I had, it would of had a profound effect on the whole rest of our marriage - a little extravagence goes a long way.<P>  so the real trick, the secret knowledge is: find out what she really wants - ask her, then ask her again in a way that makes her feel free to tell you.<P>   then DO IT!||||reg||1
